************** G E N E R A L   I N F O R M A T I O N *************5528 1451   30
                                                                  5528 1451   31
This evaluated data file is based on a software system built      5528 1451   32
around the nuclear model code TALYS [kon23], version 2.0. It is   5528 1451   33
part of a large collection of isotopic evaluations, all created by5528 1451   34
running the system with either adjusted or default input          5528 1451   35
parameters. This means that the data in the entire collection have5528 1451   36
been tested in detail for many isotopes against individual        5528 1451   37
experimental data, while for other isotopes it is only as good as 5528 1451   38
the global quality of TALYS at the moment. The mutual quality of  5528 1451   39
all individual data files is however consistent: The same set of  5528 1451   40
nuclear models is used and, equally important, the same ENDF-6    5528 1451   41
formatting procedures for each isotope. The data file has been    5528 1451   42
created automatically using the ENDF-6 format generator TEFAL.    5528 1451   43
                                                                  5528 1451   44
The resulting data file provides a complete representation of     5528 1451   45
nuclear data needed for transport, activation, damage, heating,   5528 1451   46
radioactivity, and shielding applications over the incident       5528 1451   47
neutron energy range from 1.e-11 to 200. MeV.                     5528 1451   48
                                                                  5528 1451   49
All transport and activation data for neutrons, charged particles,5528 1451   50
photons and residual nuclides are filed. This includes cross      5528 1451   51
sections, angular distributions, double-differential spectra,     5528 1451   52
isomeric production, discrete and continuum photon production     5528 1451   53
cross sections, residual production cross sections and recoils.   5528 1451   54
This general purpose evaluation can thus be used as both          5528 1451   55
transport and activation library.                                 5528 1451   56
                                                                  5528 1451   57
A complete set of covariance data is included, which is stored    5528 1451   58
in MF31-40.                                                       5528 1451   59
                                                                  5528 1451   60
