  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           5528 1451   80
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.61, compiled on         5528 1451   81
       Jan 30 2025, 17:29:54 at Villigen   , Switzerland. The RRR 5528 1451   82
       expands from 0 to 3.089159E+2 eV. A total of               5528 1451   83
       3 l-values are used and 30 resonances. The resonance       5528 1451   84
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              5528 1451   85
       The TARES database for the measured resonances is          5528 1451   86
        ->  default up to 261.000000 eV.                          5528 1451   87
       Above this energy, the ladder approach is used.            5528 1451   88
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       5528 1451   89
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          5528 1451   90
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     5528 1451   91
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    5528 1451   92
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  5528 1451   93
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   5528 1451   94
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          5528 1451   95
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       5528 1451   96
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    5528 1451   97
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       5528 1451   98
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         5528 1451   99
       The s-wave average level spacing is 11.224600 eV and       5528 1451  100
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.000156 1e-4.              5528 1451  101
