***************************** T A L Y S **************************5528 1451  130
                                                                  5528 1451  131
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   5528 1451  132
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      5528 1451  133
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    5528 1451  134
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     5528 1451  135
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  5528 1451  136
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        5528 1451  137
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    5528 1451  138
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         5528 1451  139
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      5528 1451  140
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    5528 1451  141
stored in this data file:                                         5528 1451  142
                                                                  5528 1451  143
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   5528 1451  144
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     5528 1451  145
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 5528 1451  146
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   5528 1451  147
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                5528 1451  148
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   5528 1451  149
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    5528 1451  150
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        5528 1451  151
- Recoil data                                                     5528 1451  152
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           5528 1451  153
- Total particle energy spectra                                   5528 1451  154
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      5528 1451  155
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        5528 1451  156
- Residual production cross sections                              5528 1451  157
                                                                  5528 1451  158
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            5528 1451  159
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        5528 1451  160
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   5528 1451  161
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                5528 1451  162
                                                                  5528 1451  163
